ies of D:"},{"x":0.28192,"y":0.75268,"w":0.0274,"h":0.01789,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"y 4"},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.774,"w":0.57385,"h":0.03135,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":1,"t":"xyz-equations for Corresponding uYw-equations Simplified the boundary of D for the boundary of G uYw-equations"},{"x":0.10451,"y":0.7941,"w":0.06362,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Front plane:"},{"x":0.10451,"y":0.80506,"w":0.13738,"h":0.02359,"fs":0.01023,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"x = + 1, or y = 2x −2 y 2"},{"x":0.36351,"y":0.80772,"w":0.54266,"h":0.11275,"fs":0.01279,"n":18,"k":0,"t":"x = y>2 u + y = 2y>2 = y u = 0 x = (y>2) + 1 u + y = (2y>2) + 1 = y + 1 u = 1 y = 0 2y = 0 y = 0 y = 4 2y = 4 y = 2 z = 0 3w = 0 w = 0 z = 3 3w = 3 w = 1"},{"x":0.08774,"y":0.84009,"w":0.20487,"h":0.05831,"fs":0.01151,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 15.63 The equations x = u + y, y = 2y, and z = 3w transform G into D. Reversing the transformation by the equations"},{"x":0.08774,"y":0.89285,"w":0.24331,"h":0.03625,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"u = (2x - y)>2, y = y>2, and w = z>3 transforms D into G (Example 5)."}]}